# TASK-B3 — blocks direct browser access to merchant profile.json files.
# Found during self re-verification: profile.json holds verification_status, charity
# registration numbers/country, and other non-public fields — none of this should be
# directly browsable by guessing a merchant ID's folder URL. Mirrors the exact pattern
# ADMIN_DASHBOARD_PROJECT_SUMMARY.md documents for CHAT_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR ("protected by an
# auto-written .htaccess containing Deny from all, so even though this folder is inside
# the public webroot, direct browser access by guessing its filename is blocked at the
# web server level") — same directive, reused rather than invented, per Rule 7.
Deny from all
